      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "64 TIMES SMALLER",
      "new_visual_element": "One vector, stored two ways",
      "narration": "Each image descriptor in my test set is 128 numbers, 512 bytes. To search a hundred thousand of them fast, the index sorts them into 256 cells and squeezes each one down to 8 bytes. That is 64 times smaller, and that compression is where the trouble starts.",
