    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "THE STAND-IN",
      "new_visual_element": "The search measures to a stand-in, not the vector",
      "narration": "Each vector is cut into eight pieces, and each piece is replaced by the closest of 256 learned patterns, so a single byte names it. That gives a stand-in, x-hat. The search never measures distance to your real vector. It measures to the stand-in, and the stand-in is fixed the moment the vector is stored.",
      "narration_text": "Each vector is cut into eight pieces, and each piece is replaced by the closest of 256 learned patterns, so a single byte names it. That gives a stand-in, x-hat. The search never measures distance to your real vector. It measures to the stand-in, and the stand-in is fixed the moment the vector is stored.",
      "shot": {
